In article <1237@ai.cs.utexas.edu> throop@cs.utexas.edu (David Throop) writes:

       Rings are harder to find, many of them are cursed, and the
   enchantment does NOT carry over across the polymorph (for instance, a -2
   ring of strength can turn into a +1 ring of adornment.)  Therefore, we
   remove curses from cursed rings and toss them into the pile.
       Curses can be removed from rings (and other cursed items) using holy
   water, scrolls of remove curse, wands of cancellation, or prayer.
   Normally, I don't like to use up a scroll on curse removal insamuch as
   scrolls are in shorter supply than potions; I prefer holy water.  I will
   make an exception for ghost hoards - these often contain cursed but
   positively enchanted armor.   In such cases, take a BLESSED scroll of
   remove curse and gather up as much cursed stuff as you can find and
   carry - this may mean taking off and dropping your regular armor and
   putting on the armor you found in the bones pile.  Since a blessed
   scroll of remove curse uncurses everything in your pack, the loss of one
   scroll make more sense than the use of many potions of holy water.
   Also, a wand of cancellation would strip the positive enchantments off
   the armor, which is undesirable.  NOTE: don't bother to uncurse wands,
   it doesn't make any difference if they are cursed.
      Particularly with rings, prayer may be a good way to remove curses.
   If you've slaughtered a squad of soldiers, you may have a large stack of
   cursed rings of protection.  If you don't have a wand of cancellation
   handy, and your armor is pretty good, and you're on good terms with your
   gods, you may just want to put these cursed rings on and pray at an
   alter.  They'll usually become uncursed; if not, you can still use holy
   water on them.  And prayer is a renewable resource in a way that holy
   water, scrolls and wand charges are not.  When uncursed, throw 'em on
   the polypile.

I prefer to uncurse an item by dipping it into a fountain. I only do
this if I'm reasonably powerful and won't die if snakes or deamons pop
up. Also, you should remember to take off armor which could rust if
you are sprayed by water. Nymphs are a pain-- genocide them.

